  "notes": "Menasha WI city hall and fire station (1885), HABS: a cream-brick two-storey hall with a gabled, pinnacled front on Main Street, a big plain brick rear block with a fire escape, flanked by a 1960s gabled senior centre and a modern office box; parking and lawn in between -- a downtown pulled apart by 1960s-80s renewal"
